ry similar to this what  do I use where do I start  is it this somebody told me are that  Julia  maybe Python but Python slow and there's  a lot of decisions to be made and so you  often wind up starting and looking at a  notebook like this it stays blank for a  while maybe you type in a few lines of  code execute them which is cool but  oftentimes if I'm trained not as a  software developer but maybe as a social  scientist I may not be able to install  things right off the bat but I want to  use them and explore them so look for  the tools in our industry where you can  try things without installing anything  binder was something that came out of  the desire to share research and  research papers unexpectedly it has  become very popular for sharing  demonstrations for running workshops and  it also far surpassed what we had  expected and as of last year there were  over two million binders launched on  that service and it's a free service  it's run by four people and the  community and those four people aren't  dedicated towards it it's a small  percentage of their job and you know  there's also collab and other things  which have a lot bigger infrastructure  behind it but binder has sort of become  the de facto standard for running  tutorials at conferences doing workshops  and scale we didn't really plan on it  initially so as you're looking at what  you're building what you choose for your  tools will matter at least initially  many of you might choose Jupiter lab  because it allows you to have multiple  windows  and pull out graphs things like that I'm  not going to go too far into Jupiter lab  because I think there's other talks  about it here but I'm happy to talk  about it later we'll just do a quick  maybe it's not quite  there's also interact is an alternative  tool which uses some of the Jupiter  folks including myself have helped build  a react based front-end for the notebook  and also components that can be reused  vs code we heard a little bit from th